{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-05_pennex991-q32026.htm, sha256 dc4ec9f7cf6edb7d5998299584a631342cf57ec481a9edfaec957d99a09f13fb.\nEX-99.1 2 pennex991-q32026.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1\nPENN Entertainment, Inc. Reports Third Quarter Results WYOMISSING, PA (November 5, 2026) - PENN Entertainment, Inc. (\u201cPENN\u201d or the \u201cCompany\u201d) (Nasdaq: PENN) today reported financial results for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026. Jay Snowden, Chief Executive Officer and President, said: \u201cPENN\u2019s third quarter results were highlighted by strong year-over-year growth in Retail Segment Adjusted EBITDAR, continued progress toward Interactive profitability, and further balance sheet deleveraging. Our Retail segment achieved record third quarter revenue, reflecting broad-based strength across the portfolio, including our completed development projects. Sustained revenue growth in U.S. standalone Hollywood iCasino and Canada, together with operational discipline, reinforces our confidence in achieving our full-year Adjusted EBITDA target in our Interactive segment. Importantly, the healthy operating trends we experienced across both our Retail and Interactive segments continued through October.\u201d Third Quarter Retail Segment Highlights1: \u2022Revenues of $1.5 billion \u2022Segment Adjusted EBITDAR of $501.8 million; and \u2022Segment Adjusted EBITDAR margins of 33.7%. \u201cOur Retail segment delivered better than expected revenue and Adjusted EBITDAR results, driven by same-store growth and contributions from our completed development projects,\u201d said Mr. Snowden. \u201cProperty-level performance was supported by increases in rated revenue and spend per visit across all age segments, meaningful contributions from mid- and high-worth customers, and continued growth in unrated revenue. For the third consecutive quarter, Segment Adjusted EBITDAR margins improved year-over-year. We believe the returns we are generating from investments in our portfolio highlight the opportunity across our remaining development pipeline and position us well for future growth.\u201d 1 Retail Segment consists of retail operating segments which are composed of our Northeast, South, West, and Midwest reportable segments.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Third Quarter Interactive Segment Highlights: \u2022Revenues of $348.4 million (including tax gross-up of $191.4 million); and \u2022Adjusted EBITDA loss of $18.3 million. \u201cAdjusted EBITDA in our Interactive segment improved meaningfully year-over-year, reflecting continued execution against our plan to achieve profitability. U.S. iCasino revenue growth was driven by the strength of standalone Hollywood iCasino, supported by efficient user acquisition and reinvestment. In Ontario, increased users and revenue per user contributed to revenue growth across both iCasino and online sports betting (\u201cOSB\u201d) as we continue to reinvest in one of our most attractive jurisdictions. We are also pleased with the early performance of our Alberta iCasino and OSB operations, which further expand our Canadian presence. These encouraging trends reinforce our strategic focus on U.S. iCasino and Canada as key drivers of profitable growth,\u201d concluded Mr. Snowden. Liquidity and Financial Position Total liquidity as of September 30, 2026 was $2.0 billion, including $1.0 billion of cash and cash equivalents. Traditional net debt as of September 30, 2026 was $1.8 billion.\n2\nSummary of Third Quarter Results\nFor the three months ended September 30,\n(in millions, except per share data, unaudited) 2026 2025\nRevenues $ 1,840.0 $ 1,717.3\nNet income (loss) $ 32.6 $ (865.1)\nConsolidated Adjusted EBITDA (1) $ 284.0 $ 194.9\nRent expense associated with triple net operating leases (2) $ 167.9 $ 158.1\nCash payments to our REIT Landlords under Triple Net Leases (3) $ 251.8 $ 241.9\nDiluted earnings (loss) per common share $ 0.24 $ (6.03)\n"}
